1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,032
Your agent skills end up copied into every project and every computer, and the copies drift apart.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,144
Skillstation keeps them in one Git repository you own.

3
00:00:12,494 --> 00:00:17,414
Your agents connect to it over MCP and pull the right skill, on demand.

4
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,664
You collect, edit and approve skills before any agent gets them.

5
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:32,350
In this film you install it, create your hub, and write your first skill.

6
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,532
You need Git and an agent such as Claude Code.

7
00:00:35,882 --> 00:00:38,378
Install Skillstation with one line.

8
00:00:38,728 --> 00:00:41,296
Open a new terminal, and check the version.

9
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:46,262
The hub is a folder in its own Git repository.

10
00:00:46,612 --> 00:00:51,412
Git records every change with your name and email, so set them once if you have not.

11
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:55,162
Then create the hub.

12
00:01:01,738 --> 00:01:04,666
Connect your agents once, for every project.

13
00:01:05,016 --> 00:01:07,224
The warning in the middle is expected.

14
00:01:09,338 --> 00:01:11,642
Then run doctor from any project.

15
00:01:13,138 --> 00:01:15,010
Healthy means you are ready.

16
00:01:21,638 --> 00:01:26,654
Restart your agent, open any project, and say: curate my Skillstation.

17
00:01:27,038 --> 00:01:30,206
The agent loads its curator skill once for this chat.

18
00:01:30,638 --> 00:01:34,358
A new hub has no skills yet, so it suggests your first one.

19
00:01:34,708 --> 00:01:40,060
From then on, short requests are enough, and the agent asks before it changes your hub.

20
00:01:41,538 --> 00:01:45,066
A skill is a folder with instructions your agent follows.

21
00:01:45,416 --> 00:01:49,496
Ask your agent to create one: say what it does, and give it a name.

22
00:01:49,846 --> 00:01:53,878
It writes the skill in your project and shows what it would add to the hub.

23
00:01:54,228 --> 00:01:56,100
Nothing is published yet.

24
00:02:02,138 --> 00:02:06,746
Try it with your agent: here, every commit message ends with a check line.

25
00:02:13,638 --> 00:02:16,350
When it works, publish it with one command.

26
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:19,412
Say yes to add it, and yes to activate it.

27
00:02:22,138 --> 00:02:28,186
Every agent that uses your hub gets it now, in every project, and your project's copy is closed.

28
00:02:29,386 --> 00:02:31,258
Prefer clicking?

29
00:02:31,608 --> 00:02:34,008
Start the web UI from your hub folder.

30
00:02:34,358 --> 00:02:39,134
Open a skill, edit a file, review the change, and commit it to the hub.

31
00:02:50,286 --> 00:02:55,470
Your hub can serve agents on other computers, on the same network or over Tailscale.

32
00:02:56,786 --> 00:03:01,778
On the hub computer, start the server as a background service and make a one-time code.

33
00:03:07,286 --> 00:03:11,606
On the other computer, install Skillstation and paste the line it printed.

34
00:03:19,986 --> 00:03:21,858
Doctor checks the connection.

35
00:03:24,786 --> 00:03:28,410
That computer keeps no skills: its agents ask the hub.

36
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,632
Curation stays on the hub.

37
00:03:33,786 --> 00:03:38,370
A skill made on the other computer is sent for review, and you approve it on the hub.

38
00:03:57,786 --> 00:04:03,042
Lost? skillstation status tells you the next step, and doctor tells you what is wrong.

39
00:04:04,286 --> 00:04:06,926
In a new chat, ask to curate again.

40
00:04:07,986 --> 00:04:10,146
The code and the guides are on GitHub.

41
00:04:10,496 --> 00:04:12,824
Tell us what works, and what does not.
